From bf52ada1fe94cfcf5b17718ad207c01a3145c72d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HaramBlur Contributor <contributor@example.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:27:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(settings): deduplicate defaults, harden popup
 language handling

- background.js: import DEFAULT_SETTINGS from constants.js instead of
  maintaining a second inline copy (the two copies had already drifted:
  constants.js was missing whitelist). The service worker is now loaded
  as an ES module (manifest: type=module).
- constants.js: add whitelist: [] to DEFAULT_SETTINGS so any code path
  that falls back to defaults gets a valid array.
- popup.js: fall back to English when the stored or browser language is
  not one of the supported locales. Previously Object.keys(undefined)
  threw and broke the entire popup for browsers set to e.g. de/fr/es.
  Also default the language select to 'en' when unset.
---
 manifest.json     |  3 ++-
 src/background.js | 29 +++++++++--------------------
 src/constants.js  |  1 +
 src/popup.js      | 10 ++++++++--
 4 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

